issue_comments.body:
@cyanguwa I left a few responses to your comments but with the merging of #2964 the essential point is that we if close this PR (#3470), what we lose is fused-attention availability/performance for head_dim_v ∈ {64, 128, 256} with FP16/BF16 and cuDNN < 9.26.

#2964 makes this unavailable whereas this PR makes them available, so I'm thinking of rebasing my PR which should basically translate this PR to a simple check, i.e. do not lose fused-attention availability/performance for head_dim_v ∈ {64, 128, 256} with FP16/BF16 and cuDNN < 9.26.

Sounds good ?
